    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the suite, and it passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the soft-match `possibleDuplicate` rule for `POST /api/owners`, following the codebase's established \"flag before save\" pattern (mirroring `FlagBulkSignup`/`CountNamesakes`) to keep structural impact low.\n\n**Files changed (5):**\n\n1. **New `FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 a small, self-contained function class (WMC_other \u2248 0). Iterates existing owners; if one shares the new owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` but has a different `telephone`, it sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to that owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate=false`. Runs before Save, so it sees only pre-existing owners and the flags persist for read-back on GET.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `flagPossibleDuplicate` step between `flagBulkSignup` and `save` (2 lines rewired, no existing step logic touched).\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added two fields (`possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`) plus their accessors. No existing method was modified, so the large `Owner` class's complexity isn't paid on any edited method.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only properties to the `Owner` response schema; MapStruct auto-maps them from the matching entity getters, so the mapper was untouched.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the two columns and padded the 10 positional seed inserts with the corresponding `NULL`s (the hsqldb profile is the one the tests use; matching the repo's existing convention of only maintaining that schema for these added columns).\n\nThe target test `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
